      "start_seconds": 1.05,
      "end_seconds": 5.97,
      "duration_seconds": 4.92,
      "text": "actually, doctor? Hello, I hope this is the right time"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.81,
      "end_seconds": 11.83,
      "duration_seconds": 5.02,
      "text": "okay, you're alright, take a seat what can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 12.99,
      "end_seconds": 18.49,
      "duration_seconds": 5.5,
      "text": "hello, doctor i hope it's alright if I stay in for this"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.0,
      "end_seconds": 28.64,
      "duration_seconds": 4.64,
      "text": "well, I've been having a red sticky eye"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.57,
      "end_seconds": 37.78,
      "duration_seconds": 7.21,
      "text": "how long has it been like this? I ask cos it helps me narrow things down"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 39.43,
      "end_seconds": 41.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "probably about a week yeah"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 42.39,
      "end_seconds": 50.37,
      "duration_seconds": 7.98,
      "text": "can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.11,
      "end_seconds": 66.8,
      "duration_seconds": 14.69,
      "text": "A seven out of ten, uh, I suppose. It settles a little with a clean cloth. I've also had a gritty feeling, for ten days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 75.12,
      "end_seconds": 76.73,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "Have you retired yet?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 77.39,
      "end_seconds": 82.11,
      "duration_seconds": 4.72,
      "text": "I retired from the post office two years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.9,
      "end_seconds": 86.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "Do you get out much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 87.2,
      "end_seconds": 91.85,
      "duration_seconds": 4.65,
      "text": "Not much, I mostly stay in these days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.58,
      "end_seconds": 95.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "right, do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.84,
      "end_seconds": 111.57,
      "duration_seconds": 14.73,
      "text": "Heart disease, for two years. Anxiety, for nearly five years. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing. I told my wife I'd come today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.71,
      "end_seconds": 116.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "Alright, heart disease, that matches what I have here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.13,
      "end_seconds": 130.42,
      "duration_seconds": 4.29,
      "text": "Are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 132.47,
      "end_seconds": 139.24,
      "duration_seconds": 6.77,
      "text": "Aspirin, 75 milligrams, once a day. It's escitalopram, 10 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.95,
      "end_seconds": 148.48,
      "duration_seconds": 8.53,
      "text": "has anything ever caused you a reaction? I mean any allergies these questions might sound routine, but they matter"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 150.29,
      "end_seconds": 157.58,
      "duration_seconds": 7.29,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, yes, nickel. I get a rash on my skin."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.17,
      "end_seconds": 164.77,
      "duration_seconds": 6.6,
      "text": "any blurred vision, contact lens, pain in the eye or sensitivity to light at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.07,
      "end_seconds": 168.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "No, none of those at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.05,
      "end_seconds": 172.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "How are your bowels, any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.66,
      "end_seconds": 177.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "No, that side's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 185.56,
      "end_seconds": 190.26,
      "duration_seconds": 4.7,
      "text": "Can I check a few measurements before we carry on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.08,
      "end_seconds": 203.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "So, keep your arm relaxed for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.05,
      "end_seconds": 235.75,
      "duration_seconds": 13.7,
      "text": "Okay: weight 65 kilos, pulse 74, temperature 36.6. And saturation 98 percent, BMI works out to 21.7, blood pressure 115 over 68, height 173 centimetres."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 236.84,
      "end_seconds": 240.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "Right, let's have a proper look at you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.3,
      "end_seconds": 243.93,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "let me feel here"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.58,
      "end_seconds": 267.16,
      "duration_seconds": 6.58,
      "text": "The white of the eye is pink with some sticky discharge, and your pupil is normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 272.68,
      "end_seconds": 297.47,
      "duration_seconds": 24.79,
      "text": "all finished, thank you let me tell you where I've got to the most likely explanation is infective conjunctivitis that's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more it could also be allergic conjunctivitis, so we'll keep that open wash your hands often and don't share towels have I covered everything you wanted?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 298.83,
      "end_seconds": 300.57,
      "duration_seconds": 1.74,
      "text": "that's clear, thanks"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 302.58,
      "end_seconds": 303.98,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "Take care now."
    }
  ]
